menu "NeuroEdge OTA (FR-OTA, TSK-S6-01..04)"

    config NEUROEDGE_OTA
        bool "Enable firmware update (A/B, RSA-signed; off by default)"
        default n
        help
            Links the HTTP(S) update path. Without it the device still honours
            A/B rollback when built with CONFIG_BOOTLOADER_APP_ROLLBACK_ENABLE,
            but it never fetches an image: an unsigned developer build cannot
            accept OTA at all.

            An update build layers sdkconfig.ota on sdkconfig.defaults; the RSA
            signing key stays out of the repository (docs/user/nap-firmware.md,
            section 6). The image is verified with the key that signed the
            running app before anything is switched.

    if NEUROEDGE_OTA

        config NEUROEDGE_OTA_URL
            string "Update URL (http:// or https://; empty disables the check)"
            default ""
            help
                Any open HTTP(S) endpoint serving a signed app image; no
                NeuroEdge service or account is involved. Plain HTTP is allowed
                because the image signature is the integrity check; it gives no
                confidentiality. A URL stored in NVS (namespace ne_ota, key
                url) overrides this at runtime.

        config NEUROEDGE_OTA_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS
            int "HTTP operation timeout (ms)"
            default 20000
            range 1000 120000

        config NEUROEDGE_OTA_ETH
            bool "Bring up Ethernet (QEMU open_eth) for the update check"
            depends on NEUROEDGE_SKIP_NETWORK
            default n
            help
                QEMU emulates no Wi-Fi; sdkconfig.qemu_ota selects this so the
                check runs over QEMU's user-mode network (the host is
                10.0.2.2). On the board the Wi-Fi stack main.c brings up is
                used, and this must stay off.

        config NEUROEDGE_OTA_TEST_BOOTLOOP
            bool "TEST ONLY: reset before this image can be marked valid"
            default n
            help
                For the rollback test (scripts/qemu_ota.sh): the image boots,
                resets itself before the gate self-test, and the bootloader
                rolls back to the previous app on the next boot — the crash /
                boot-loop path of FR-OTA-02. A reset, not a panic: Espressif
                QEMU 9.0 hangs in the panic handler before it prints or
                reboots (measured), so a panic here would prove nothing.
                Never enable this in a shipped image.

        config NEUROEDGE_OTA_TEST_FAIL_SELFTEST
            bool "TEST ONLY: fail the boot self-test before marking valid"
            default n
            help
                For the rollback test (scripts/qemu_ota.sh): the image fails
                the gate self-test, marks itself invalid and reboots into the
                previous app. Never enable this in a shipped image.

    endif
endmenu
